UID:10001534-1787392800-1787400000@houstonarboretum.org
SUMMARY:A Year in the Wildlife Garden
DESCRIPTION:$22 member / $37 nonmemberAges 12+\, minors must be accompanied by an adult \n\n\n\nWhat’s the best time to plant wildflowers\, put up a birdhouse\, or clean up the garden after a freeze? With a little understanding of nature’s rhythms\, you can plan your year to maximize wildlife benefits and minimize your stress. In this class we’ll talk through a year in the wildlife garden and send you home with a calendar of to-dos for each season. \n\n\n\nPlease dress for the weather and wear walking shoes. \n\n\n\n\nregister online
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/a-year-in-the-wildlife-garden/
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Nature & Wildlife,Plants & Gardening
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Pollinator-Garden-Kelsey-Low.jpg
END:VEVENT
